- Upstream PRs applied (all unmerged upstream as of 2026-10-31):
  - #37 ml_derp_connect(): check mbedTLS setup errors and free TLS state on every failure.
    The PR uses `goto fail` without defining the label; the label was added here, and the
    nine failure paths after the HTTP upgrade (ServerKey/ClientInfo/ServerInfo) also go there
  - #30 per-packet datapath logging moved to DEBUG (the ml_derp.c HEARTBEAT hunk was already
    applied locally)
  - #29 ML_DERP_REGION is a Kconfig option (sdkconfig.defaults sets 7, Tokyo)
  - #28 commit 2 only (0de347e): udp_sendto, udp_new, netif_list/netif_set_up and
    netif_set_link_up/down run on tcpip_thread. Commits 1 and 3 are the same as the
    netif->input fix above
  - #31 cache the DISCO X25519 shared secret
  - #32 deeper WG/DISCO RX queues, blocking receive in ml_wg_mgr, drain the DISCO socket
    (the trailing vTaskDelay hunk was applied by hand after #30)
  - #21 don't install unvalidated peer endpoints at peer-add (DERP until DISCO validates)
- Known remaining: wireguardif_network_rx() still runs on the wg_mgr task, so peer keypair
  state is shared with the tcpip_thread output path without a lock (headboard issue #1)
